        "short_description": "Placeholder for an annual six-nation rugby union championship: a single round robin of five rounds, every nation plays every other once, home advantage alternating each year, bonus-point table (4/2/0, try-margin bonus, losing bonus within 7, extra points for winning every match). Rename it and its six nations during onboarding."
      },
      "lore": [
        {
          "title": "House rules",
          "content": "Scoring: win 4, draw 2, loss 0; try bonus 1 for scoring at least three more tries than the opponent; losing bonus 1 for losing by seven or fewer; a nation that wins all five matches gets 3 extra points. tiebreakers: h2h_first (head-to-head table_points, head-to-head points_difference, points_difference, tries_for, points_for, disciplinary record, drawing of lots). Each season is five rounds over seven weekends with two rest weekends (not scored byes); home and away alternate per pairing each year. Edit this chunk to the competition's published rules and record who asked and when.",
